  "date": "2022-03",
  "title": "Food 4 Though Learn More About Sustainable Nutrition",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Workshops",
      "text": "The Food4Thought trade fair will be held from 3 to 5 April on Hönggerberg campus. The event focuses on climate-friendly nutrition: visitors can get inspired by ETH spin-offs, start-ups and student projects and learn about practical concepts and real-life products that can help them eat in a more climate- and environmentally-friendly way.\n\nThe 17 stands at Food4Thought offer activities such as tastings to get acquainted with new kinds of food and workshops for producing your own products. Researchers at the lunchtime “Meet the Scientist” event will share insights into ongoing projects dedicated to climate-friendly food. You can also learn more about student products and what is already being done on the ETH campus to make sustainable nutrition a reality."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Workshops",
      "text": "There will be three interactive workshops for visitors:\n\nZwingliPilz The ZwingliPilz workshop teaches participants how to grow delicious gourmet mushrooms from waste that contains cellulose.\n\nGreenioty At the Greenioty workshop, you can build a small system for cultivating your own microgreens at home. ACKR Visit the ACKR workshop to learn how to preserve vegetables by canning and fermenting them at home.\n\nYou can find more details on dates and times on the event website . Please note that it is required to register for workshops in advance."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Awareness campaign kicks off",
      "text": "The Food4Thought trade fair will be held on 3 April as part of Treffpunkt Science City and will continue on 4 and 5 April (Monday/Tuesday). The event kicks off the awareness campaign that ETH is launching as part of the Swiss federal government’s Exemplary Energy and Climate initiative (see box)."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Staffnet",
      "text": "The Exemplary Energy and Climate initiative requires ETH to raise awareness in its community about ecological issues between 2021 and 2030. The participation of ETH Zurich is mandatory due to being part of the ETH Domain, and a different topic is chosen to focus on every year. The idea is to acquaint members of the ETH community with initiatives and projects that are being implemented at the university.\n\nThe launch of the awareness campaign was delayed by one year due to the coronavirus pandemic. It is now scheduled to start this year. Sustainable nutrition is the topic in the spotlight for 2022, making the Food4Thought fair the perfect venue for kicking off the campaign.\n\nThe Exemplary Energy and Climate initiative is part of the federal government’s Energy Strategy 2050 . It is aimed at the most important Swiss public service providers who want to promote innovation and serve as an example when it comes to environmental issues."
    }
  ],
